<title>AUSTRALIA: KPN FUNDS TNT BID BY CREDIT FACILITY.</title>
<headline>KPN FUNDS TNT BID BY CREDIT FACILITY.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch post and telecoms group</p>
<p>Koninklijke PTT Nederland NV said on Wednesday it would fund its</p>
<p>A$2.0 billion bid for Australian transport group TNT Ltd</p>
<p>from working capital and a 2.25 billion guilder (A$1.7</p>
<p>billion) revolving credit facility arranged and underwritten by</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs.</p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, KPN said it would bid A$2.45 per share</p>
<p>for TNT, valuing the group at A$2 billion, a 48 percent premium</p>
<p>to its current market capitalisation.</p>
<p>&quot;KPN is financing the offer and providing working capital</p>
<p>facilities for the combined group by means of existing cash</p>
<p>resources and a 2.25 billion guilder (A$1.7 billion) revolving</p>
<p>credit facility, which has been arranged and fully underwritten</p>
<p>by Goldman Sachs,&quot; KPN said in a joint statement with TNT</p>
<p>announcing the bid.</p>
<p>TNT said it recommended shareholders accept the offer.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
